A. Commit message:
dmaengine: loongson2-apb: Change GENMASK to GENMASK_ULL for 32-bit toolchain compatibility

B. Change summary:
This patch changes the usage of GENMASK to GENMASK_ULL in the definition of LDMA_CONFIG_MASK to ensure compatibility with 32-bit toolchains. This change addresses a smatch static checker warning and prevents build issues when accessing bits beyond 31.

C. Compatibility Risk:
High

D. Fixed Code:
diff --git a/drivers/dma/loongson2-apb-dma.c b/drivers/dma/loongson2-apb-dma.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c528f02b9f848
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/dma/loongson2-apb-dma.c
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+#include <linux/bitops.h>
+#include <linux/dmaengine.h>
+
+/* Bitfields in config field */
+#define LDMA_ASK_VALID		BIT(2)
+#define LDMA_START		BIT(3) /* DMA start operation */
+#define LDMA_STOP		BIT(4) /* DMA stop operation */
+#define LDMA_CONFIG_MASK	GENMASK_ULL(4, 0) /* DMA controller config bits mask */
+
+/* Bitfields in ndesc_addr field of HW descriptor */
+#define LDMA_DESC_EN		BIT(0) /*1: The next descriptor is valid */
+
+/* Rest of the driver code remains unchanged */